      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E004",
        "passage_id": "P002",
        "quote": "Contrary to the defendant's contention, the court's prior order regarding production of the entire surveillance video, which was denied without prejudice, has no preclusive effect. Although defendants were not required to mop continuously, and there was testimony that they usually mopped when it rained, there was no evidence that they mopped at all on the day of the accident",
